:{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in:\n  - 4.4.1.stable\n  - 4.5.dev [b89c47b]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.1.1.stable - Windows 11 (build 26100) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 Laptop - Intel i7-12700H (20 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nRelated to: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106840\n\nIf a script uses the same variable name as a `@GDScript` constant, the former is used. However, the editor hints at the `@GDScript` constant instead of the local variable.\n\nIt is also weird that the local variable can override the `@GDScript` constant without warnings.\n\nI think the local variable should hide the global constant and print a warning, similar to how local variables can hide the property of a base class and print a warning:\n\n```\nW 0:00:01:727   The local variable \"position\" is shadowing an already-declared property in the base class \"Node2D\".\n  <GDScript Error>SHADOWED_VARIABLE_BASE_CLASS\n  <GDScript Source>main.gd:11\n```\n\nNotes:\n- happens regardless of being an `Autoload` or not\n-  happens regardless of having `class_name` or not\n\nScreenshots:\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7c695b4b-6a49-4270-bdd3-c97ece047087)\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/da0a48b0-630d-466f-be32-d46e73988fe9)\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Open the attached project and run it in the editor\n2. Hover the cursor over the `PI` local variable\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n(probably not project-dependent)\n[bug_localvarhidesglobalconst.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20512164/bug_localvarhidesglobalconst.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","